{"post_stream": {"posts": [{"id": 203652, "name": "meterwatcher", "username": "meterwatcher", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forum.valuepickr.com/meterwatcher/{size}/1001_2.png", "created_at": "2019-12-27T04:14:27.337Z", "cooked": "<p>Starting a dedicated thread for Genus Power since it keeps coming up in portfolio discussions here but has no thread of its own. I have spent a few weeks with the annual reports and am sharing my notes below; corrections from members who have followed the company longer are welcome.</p>\n<h2><a name=\"p-203652-what-the-company-does-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-203652-what-the-company-does-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a>What the company does</h2>\n<p>Genus makes electricity meters, from basic static meters to smart and prepaid ones, and also takes on installation and maintenance work for power distribution utilities. Most of its customers are state-owned distribution companies, so tender cycles and payment discipline at the states matter a lot.</p>\n<p>The company reports two segments:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Metering\n<ul>\n<li>The bulk of revenue</li>\n<li>Single-phase and three-phase meters for homes, shops and factories</li>\n<li>Smart, prepaid and audit meters, plus meter testing equipment</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Engineering and contracts\n<ul>\n<li>A smaller share of revenue</li>\n<li>Turnkey work on power transmission and distribution projects</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><a name=\"p-203652-things-to-track-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-203652-things-to-track-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a>Things I plan to track</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Receivable days, since utilities are often slow to pay</li>\n<li>Order inflow from smart meter tenders, and whether it is won at sensible prices</li>\n<li>Gross margin, given how much of the bill of materials is electronic components</li>\n<li>Related party transactions and any capital that goes into group companies</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><a name=\"p-203652-open-questions-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-203652-open-questions-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a>Open questions</h2>\n<p>How much equity will the project companies need over the next few years, and will it come from internal accruals or fresh borrowing? And how sticky is the maintenance revenue once a rollout is finished?</p>\n<p>Disc: small tracking position, not a recommendation.</p>", "post_number": 1, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 182, "updated_at": "2019-12-27T04:14:27.337Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 5784, "reads": 2413, "readers_count": 2412, "score": 29577.6, "yours": false, "topic_id": 26679, "topic_slug": "genus-power-smart-metering", "display_username": "meterwatcher", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [], "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 12}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 16146, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": false, "wiki": false, "post_url": "/t/genus-power-smart-metering/26679/1", "actionable_count": 0, "actioned": false, "can_undo_actionable": false, "can_toggle_actionable": false, "show_actionable": true, "insightful_count": 0, "insightfuled": false, "can_undo_insightful": false, "can_toggle_insightful": false, "show_insightful": true, "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 12}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 12, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 208156, "name": "longterm_reader", "username": "longterm_reader", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forum.valuepickr.com/longterm_reader/{size}/1002_2.png", "created_at": "2020-02-01T07:00:48.392Z", "cooked": "<p>Thanks for putting this together. Receivables are the point I would watch most closely: a large order book only helps if the utilities actually pay on time.</p>", "post_number": 2, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 182, "updated_at": "2020-02-01T07:00:48.392Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 4, "reads": 656, "readers_count": 655, "score": 196.2, "yours": false, "topic_id": 26679, "topic_slug": "genus-power-smart-metering", "display_username": "longterm_reader", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 3}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 15870, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": false, "wiki": false, "post_url": "/t/genus-power-smart-metering/26679/2", "actionable_count": 0, "actioned": false, "can_undo_actionable": false, "can_toggle_actionable": false, "show_actionable": true, "insightful_count": 0, "insightfuled": false, "can_undo_insightful": false, "can_toggle_insightful": false, "show_insightful": true, "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 3}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 3, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}], "stream": [203652, 208156, 208467, 233853, 246044, 257706, 261654, 266066, 296736, 296737, 310290, 310769, 319443, 327725, 333988, 334894, 334964